#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="tmdb_movie_400571" tvg-name="Artful Kate" tvg-logo="https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/uNRhrScybFBCN1TH7CrYHWSreey.jpg" tvg-type="movie" tvg-genre="Midnight Cult Cinema" tvg-description="The story opens with a pretty love scene between the Lieutenant and his betrothed, Kate Stanley. Hammond is ordered to join his regiment in Cuba and Kate is heartbroken. He tells her they must part, and the girl decides to be brave. She exacts from him a promise that he will be true to her, and not indulge in any flirtations with the dark-eyed senoritas she has been told lure men from their vows of constancy in the land of flowers. Hammond is only too willing to swear eternal constancy. Kate places in his watch case a photograph of herself, kisses her manly soldier, and the leave-taking is very affectionate. The scene reverts to Cuba, Lieutenant Hammond arrives, and is impressed with the country. Kate, having relatives in Havana, receives an invitation to pay them a visit and eagerly accepts, thinking she will meet her lover. She is apprised of his arrival at Havana, and, knowing the predilection of soldiers to flirt, resolves to investigate." tvg-year="1911" tvg-cast="Mary Pickford, Owen Moore, Charles Arling" tvg-director="Thomas H. Ince" group-title="Midnight Cult Cinema",Artful Kate
https://download.blender.org/demo/movies/Sintel.2010.720p.mkv

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="tmdb_movie_9761" tvg-name="Elephants Dream" tvg-logo="https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/9zROtU9TkpZQrOuEaMAp68FOWLK.jpg" tvg-backdrop="https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w1280/9bJDwuhza19HQcYA99FeslLYmUm.jpg" tvg-type="movie" tvg-genre="Midnight Cult Cinema" tvg-description="Elephants Dream is the story of two strange characters exploring a capricious and seemingly infinite machine. The elder, Proog, acts as a tour-guide and protector, happily showing off the sights and dangers of the machine to his initially curious but increasingly skeptical protege Emo. As their journey unfolds we discover signs that the machine is not all Proog thinks it is, and his guiding takes on a more desperate aspect.  Elephants Dream is a story about communication and fiction, made purposefully open-ended as the world’s first 3D animated “Open movie”. The film itself is released under the Creative Commons license, along with the entirety of the production files used to make it (roughly 7 Gigabytes of data). The software used to make the movie is the free/open source animation suite Blender along with other open source software, thus allowing the movie to be remade, remixed and re-purposed with only a computer and the data on the DVD or download." tvg-year="2006" tvg-cast="Tygo Gernandt, Cas Jansen" tvg-director="Bassam Kurdali" group-title="Midnight Cult Cinema",Elephants Dream
https://download.blender.org/demo/movies/Sintel.2010.720p.mkv

